{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-10-30T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Winter brings a familiar rhythm to Bosque del Apache National Wildlife Refuge in New Mexico. The cranes arrive, wetlands fill with birds, and this area becomes a hub for seasonal wildlife. Established in 1939, the 57,331-acre sanctuary was created to provide a protected stopover for migrating waterfowl. Its wetlands, fields and waterways now support wildlife throughout the year. Sandhill cranes, seen in today's image, are especially associated with the refuge during winter.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnCranes_EN-IN9113460841_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnCranes_EN-IN9113460841_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Time to fly high","Title":"Sandhill cranes, Bosque del Apache National Wildlife Refuge, New Mexico, USA","Copyright":"© Terry St.Louis/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/34.384147,-106.900263/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=34.384147,-106.900263;S9;Bosque del Apache National Wildlife Refuge, New Mexico&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261030_AutumnCranes\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sandhill+Cranes&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261029_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261030_AutumnCranes"},"Ssd":"20261030","Name":"AutumnCranes","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9113460841","FullDateString":"30 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As morning mist drifts among the standing stones of Avebury in Wiltshire, England, the scene feels almost timeless. These ancient megaliths form part of one of the world's most remarkable prehistoric landscapes, centred on a vast Neolithic monument built around 4,500 years ago. Avebury contains the world's largest prehistoric stone circle, as well as a massive henge and stone avenues extending into the surrounding countryside. Together with nearby monuments such as Silbury Hill and West Kennet Avenue, it forms part of an extensive Neolithic complex that has fascinated generations of visitors, researchers and archaeologists.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AveburyStones_EN-IN9660577333_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AveburyStones_EN-IN9660577333_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where mist meets millennia","Title":"Standing stones at Avebury in Wiltshire, England","Copyright":"© George W Johnson/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/51.42898,-1.854909/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=51.42898,-1.854909;S9;Avebury, Wiltshire, England&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261029_AveburyStones\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Avebury+henge+Wiltshire&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261028_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261029_AveburyStones"},"Ssd":"20261029","Name":"AveburyStones","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9660577333","FullDateString":"29 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What stories could these walls tell? Rising above eastern Bohemia in Czechia, Kunětická hora Castle has witnessed centuries of history. Dating to the late 14th century, the castle gradually evolved into an impressive fortress and noble residence. Its elevated position offered commanding views of the surrounding countryside and helped make it an important stronghold.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KuneticeCastle_EN-IN9209042094_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KuneticeCastle_EN-IN9209042094_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where history stands watch","Title":"Kunětická hora Castle, Bohemia, Czechia","Copyright":"© Marek Saroch/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/50.080287,15.811615/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=50.080287,15.811615;S9;Kunětická hora Castle, Czechia&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261028_KuneticeCastle\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Kuneticka+hora+Castle&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261027_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261028_KuneticeCastle"},"Ssd":"20261028","Name":"KuneticeCastle","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9209042094","FullDateString":"28 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Reflected in calm water and glowing in the light of the setting sun, this grove of pond cypress creates a striking display of colour and symmetry. Native to the southeastern United States, the species is associated with shallow ponds, depressions and wetland habitats. This image was captured in Georgia, where these trees can be found in places such as the Okefenokee Swamp and other low-lying wetlands.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PondCypress_EN-IN8944704657_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PondCypress_EN-IN8944704657_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Nature's golden mirror","Title":"A grove of pond cypress trees with autumn foliage, Georgia, United States","Copyright":"© Chris Moore/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Pond cypress can develop knobby root structures known as 'knees' that rise above the water or soil around the tree.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261027_PondCypress\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Pond+cypress&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261026_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261027_PondCypress"},"Ssd":"20261027","Name":"PondCypress","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8944704657","FullDateString":"27 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Bulgaria's Western Rhodope Mountains, autumn leaves gather beside the rushing waters of Sitovo Waterfall. Near the village of Sitovo, southwest of Plovdiv, the falls tumble beneath an old stone bridge whose arch frames the cascades like a storybook scene. Moss-covered stones and pine trees add shades of green to the autumn landscape, while fallen leaves gather along the water's edge or drift through its pools. The falls become especially lively after rain and during spring snowmelt, when the surrounding woodland echoes with the sound of rushing water.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SitovoWaterfall_EN-IN8441319721_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SitovoWaterfall_EN-IN8441319721_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Nature's autumn soundtrack","Title":"Autumn waterfalls near Sitovo, Plovdiv Province, Bulgaria","Copyright":"© Nadya85/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/41.926863,24.615841/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=41.926863,24.615841;S9;Sitovo, Plovdiv Province, Bulgaria&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261026_SitovoWaterfall\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sitovo+Plovdiv+Bulgaria&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261025_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261026_SitovoWaterfall"},"Ssd":"20261026","Name":"SitovoWaterfall","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8441319721","FullDateString":"26 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What if a city's busiest street had no road? In Venice, Italy, traffic flows along the Grand Canal, a 3.9-kilometre waterway that winds through the city in a giant reverse S-shape. Known to locals as the Canalazzo, it is Venice's main water-traffic corridor, carrying vaporetti, water taxis, gondolas, police boats and other vessels. The canal follows the course of an ancient river that once flowed into the Venetian Lagoon.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VeniceSunrise_EN-IN8305689376_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VeniceSunrise_EN-IN8305689376_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The road that runs on water","Title":"Grand Canal in Venice, Italy","Copyright":"© Juan Romero/Cavan Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/45.435337,12.32783/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=45.435337,12.32783;S9;Grand Canal, Venice, Italy&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261025_VeniceSunrise\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Grand+Canal+Venice&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261024_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261025_VeniceSunrise"},"Ssd":"20261025","Name":"VeniceSunrise","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8305689376","FullDateString":"25 Oct, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today we're inside the Royal Portuguese Cabinet of Reading in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, where the humble act of opening a book took on grand architectural ambitions. Founded in 1837 by 43 Portuguese immigrants, just 15 years after Brazil's independence, the institution eventually moved into the building seen here, completed half a century later in a lavish Neo-Manueline style. Shelves soar over 20 metres around a vast reading room, crowned by a monumental stained-glass skylight that makes daylight part of the design.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PortugueseLibrary_EN-IN8235557432_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PortugueseLibrary_EN-IN8235557432_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":false},"Headline":"Bookishly extravagant","Title":"Royal Portuguese Cabinet of Reading, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil","Copyright":"© Antonio Salaverry/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-22.905431,-43.182116/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-22.905431,-43.182116;S9;Royal Portuguese Cabinet of Reading, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261024_PortugueseLibrary\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Royal+Portuguese+Cabinet+of+Reading&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261023_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261024_PortugueseLibrary"},"Ssd":"20261024","Name":"PortugueseLibrary","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8235557432","FullDateString":"24 Oct, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A volcano, a rainforest and a bamboo grove? Haleakalā National Park on Maui has all three. Spanning Maui from its 3,055-metre summit to the coast, the park protects landscapes that change dramatically with elevation, rainfall and temperature. It was established in 1916 as part of Hawaii National Park and became its own national park in 1961. The name Haleakalā translates to 'House of the Sun', reflecting the Hawaiian mo'olelo of Māui capturing the Sun to lengthen the day.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PipiwaiTrail_EN-IN0566152296_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PipiwaiTrail_EN-IN0566152296_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A green tunnel through Maui","Title":"Bamboo forest, Pīpīwai Trail, Haleakalā National Park, Maui, Hawaii, USA","Copyright":"© MNStudio/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/20.760987,-156.155095/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=20.760987,-156.155095;S9;Haleakalā National Park, Maui, Hawaii&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261106_PipiwaiTrail\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Haleakala+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261105_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261106_PipiwaiTrail"},"Ssd":"20261106","Name":"PipiwaiTrail","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"0566152296","FullDateString":"6 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A simple wooden stile leads into one of England's most celebrated landscapes. The Lake District, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, is a patchwork of shimmering lakes, rugged fells and centuries-old stone walls, all shaped by both nature and farming traditions.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.StileCrossing_EN-IN0635462552_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.StileCrossing_EN-IN0635462552_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"One step closer to the summit","Title":"Wooden stile at a stone wall, Black Crag, Lake District, England","Copyright":"© Alex Treadway/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/54.460861,-3.08875/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=54.460861,-3.08875;S9;Lake District, England&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261105_StileCrossing\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+District&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261104_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261105_StileCrossing"},"Ssd":"20261105","Name":"StileCrossing","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"0635462552","FullDateString":"5 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"People paddle through a glowing maze of bald cypress in Xuancheng, Anhui, where autumn transforms flooded woodlands into a tapestry of amber, copper and deep rust. Known scientifically as 'Taxodium distichum', bald cypress is unusual among conifers because it sheds its soft, feathery needles each fall, turning reddish-brown before they drop.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnChina_EN-IN9898936239_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnChina_EN-IN9898936239_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Paddling a painted forest","Title":"People rowing among colourful bald cypress, Xuancheng, Anhui, China","Copyright":"© Jackal Pan/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/30.9525,118.75528/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=30.9525,118.75528;S9;Xuancheng, Anhui, China&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261104_AutumnChina\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=bald+cypress&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261103_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261104_AutumnChina"},"Ssd":"20261104","Name":"AutumnChina","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9898936239","FullDateString":"4 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Lake Braies sits almost 1,500 metres above sea level in the Dolomites of South Tyrol, northern Italy. Surrounded by forest and the dramatic peaks of the Fanes-Sennes-Braies Nature Park, the lake is known for its striking green and blue waters. A 3.5-kilometre trail circles the shore, while traditional wooden rowing boats offer another way to take in the scenery. The lake is also a starting point for several mountain walks, including the Dolomites' famous Alta Via 1.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AlpineBraies_EN-IN9491975263_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AlpineBraies_EN-IN9491975263_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Peace among the peaks","Title":"Lake Braies, Fanes‑Sennes‑Braies Nature Park, Dolomites, Italy","Copyright":"© leonid_tit/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/46.693566,12.084606/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=46.693566,12.084606;S9;Lake Braies, Fanes‑Sennes‑Braies Nature Park&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261103_AlpineBraies\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+Braies+Dolomites&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261102_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261103_AlpineBraies"},"Ssd":"20261103","Name":"AlpineBraies","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9491975263","FullDateString":"3 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"These polar bears are gathering along the shores of Hudson Bay in Manitoba, Canada, waiting for sea ice to form so they can head back out to hunt seals. That annual spectacle inspired Polar Bear Week, observed during the first week of November, a celebration of the Arctic's largest land predator. Polar bears are powerful swimmers, expert hunters and remarkably adapted to life in one of Earth's harshest environments. Yet shrinking sea ice means many spend longer on land, making it harder to find food and raising the risk of encounters with people.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HudsonBear_EN-IN9299365522_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HudsonBear_EN-IN9299365522_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A future written in ice","Title":"Polar bear and cubs by Hudson Bay, Manitoba, Canada","Copyright":"© Danita Delimont/Adobe Stock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"In a single season, a polar bear may cover more than 1,000 kilometres while searching for food and suitable ice.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261102_HudsonBear\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Polar+Bear+Week&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261101_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261102_HudsonBear"},"Ssd":"20261102","Name":"HudsonBear","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9299365522","FullDateString":"2 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today we're enjoying the misty views sweeping across the Black Forest, which stretches for around 160 kilometres across south-west Germany, bringing together wooded hills, deep valleys, lakes and charming towns. Its highest point, Feldberg, rises to 1,493 metres, while the Black Forest is also the starting point for the Danube and Neckar rivers. There's plenty of history and tradition here too. Forestry has long played an important role in the region, while its centuries-old clockmaking heritage helped make the distinctive cuckoo clock famous far beyond Germany.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SchwarzwaldAutumn_EN-IN9123894203_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SchwarzwaldAutumn_EN-IN9123894203_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Mist among the trees","Title":"Black Forest, Baden-Württemberg, Germany","Copyright":"© Britus/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/48.286722,8.215281/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=48.286722,8.215281;S9;Black Forest, Baden-Württemberg&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261101_SchwarzwaldAutumn\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Black+Forest+Germany&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261031_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261101_SchwarzwaldAutumn"},"Ssd":"20261101","Name":"SchwarzwaldAutumn","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9123894203","FullDateString":"1 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Forget the fog machine. Frankfurt, Germany, has something far more effective: a Gothic cathedral with a tower that looks ready for a midnight séance. St Bartholomew's Cathedral, seen here, has the medieval silhouette Halloween practically ordered for itself. But the festival's own history is even stranger.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FrankfurtHalloween_EN-IN8941917618_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FrankfurtHalloween_EN-IN8941917618_1920x1